# busybox init table for the deterministic-vmm Alpine container guest.
#
# This OVERRIDES Alpine's stock /etc/inittab (which drives OpenRC + getty on
# tty1-6 — neither of which this minimal RAM-only serial guest uses). Our /init
# does all the setup (mounts, clock, container store, self-test) and then execs
# busybox init, so there is no ::sysinit entry here.
#
# Why busybox init (not a bare `exec /bin/sh`): a plain shell as PID 1 dies on
# `exit` (kernel panic "Attempted to kill init!"), and it ignores the
# SIGUSR2/SIGTERM that busybox `poweroff`/`reboot` send to PID 1 — so the guest
# could not be shut down by name. busybox init instead:
#   * RESPAWNS the shell, so `exit` yields a fresh prompt (VMM keeps running);
#   * relays `poweroff` -> reboot(RB_POWER_OFF) -> the kernel's `cli; hlt`
#     terminal halt (no ACPI), which the VMM recognizes as a clean stop (0);
#   * relays `reboot`   -> reboot(RB_AUTOBOOT) -> triple fault (reboot=t) ->
#     KVM_EXIT_SHUTDOWN -> the VMM stops (0).

# Interactive shell on the serial console (/dev/console == ttyS0). respawn ==
# restart it whenever it exits.
::respawn:/bin/sh

# On shutdown/reboot, flush and unmount read-only before the machine resets.
::shutdown:/bin/busybox umount -a -r

# Ctrl-Alt-Del (if it ever reaches us) reboots rather than doing nothing.
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
